stuff and bonus videos.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:58.290
Friday will be Constantine.

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:01.030
That’s the fourth DC Comics TV Show.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:04.960
It’s starting October 24th at 10PM on NBC.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:08.820
The number one reason you need to watch this
is the same as Arrow and the Flash, it is

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:13.280
going to heavily feature characters from the
comic books and will fill that magic gap in

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:15.910
the DC Universe movies and tv.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:19.570
Right now magic doesn’t exist on Arrow or
the Flash.

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:23.010
So Constantine is like the magic-based Comic
Book show.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.760
They even just cast the Spectre.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:28.930
I haven’t done a lot of bonus videos for
this yet, but I will start in the next week.

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:35.260
I got to see the first episode at comic con
so I’ll do a non-spoilery review.

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:44.630
Then Saturdays, Doctor Who Series 8 will continue
until November 8th on BBC America or the BBC

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:46.100
depending on where you live.

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:52.090
New episodes air in the UK at 7:30 GMT and
9PM on BBC America.

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:55.521
If you’re not watching it yet, the episodes
are made to stand alone by themselves, so

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:59.080
you don’t have to worry about not having
watch everything that has come before.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:02.910
I feel like a lot of people new to the fandom
get put off by the sheer quantity of Doctor

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:04.220
Who there is.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:07.670
But I do a ton of bonus videos.

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:10.340
So those should help you get up to speed.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:13.330
Of all the Science Fiction shows I do, this
